# docs/ — durable project knowledge

## Purpose

The project's written memory for humans and agents: why it exists, what to build
next, how it was decided, and what was learned. Not code, not generated output.

## Scope & Boundaries

- Owns: `brief.md` (why and for whom), `lessons.md` (the self-annealing backlog),
  `plan/work-plan.md` (the dispatch board, when the planning loop is used),
  `specs/<workstream>.md` (one owning spec per workstream), `decisions/` (one file
  per decision that should not be re-litigated), `wireframes/` (UI sketches).
- Does NOT own: how a directory works (its own `AGENTS.md`), how a skill runs (its
  `SKILL.md`), pending cross-session actions (`HANDOFF.md` at the root), or
  generated reports and run results.

## Conventions

- Answer first (BLUF): the first lines of every doc carry its conclusion and status.
- Every spec and plan row has a dated status header verified against the code.
- A spec's acceptance criteria are commands or observable states, never "works well".
- Delete stale text instead of explaining history; git is the archive.
- `lessons.md` is edited through `anneal.py`, not by hand.
